From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: conda-forge nodejs-feedstock <noreply@conda-forge.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Guard V8's JSON SIMD path on scalar-only Highway targets

V8's fast JSON stringifier unconditionally instantiates AppendStringSIMD,
which builds a hw::FixedTag<SrcChar, 16> and therefore needs a Highway
target that can supply a 16-lane byte vector.

On linux-riscv64 no such target is selected. conda-forge builds with
-march=rv64imafdc, so there is no V extension and HWY_RVV is unavailable,
and Highway's fallback EMU128 is disabled by HWY_BROKEN_EMU128, which
detect_targets.h sets for GCC < 16 (conda-forge pins GCC 15). That leaves
HWY_SCALAR, where HWY_LANES(T) is 1, and the build fails:

  shared-inl.h:369:27: error: static assertion failed: Too many lanes
    note: the comparison reduces to '(16 <= 1)'
  shared-inl.h:234:24: error: static assertion failed: Out of range
    note: the comparison reduces to '(16 <= 8)'
  json-stringifier.cc:3401:30: error: no matching function for call to
    'Set(hwy::N_SCALAR::FixedTag<unsigned char, 16>&, int)'

Wrap the dispatch in "if constexpr" so the SIMD path is only instantiated
when the static target can satisfy it. AppendStringSWAR is already a
complete implementation and handles arbitrary lengths, so scalar-only
targets simply lose the SIMD speedup. Targets that do provide 16-byte
vectors are unaffected -- the generated assembly is unchanged.
---
 deps/v8/src/json/json-stringifier.cc | 22 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/deps/v8/src/json/json-stringifier.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/json/json-stringifier.cc
@@ -3333,9 +3333,28 @@
 bool FastJsonStringifier<Char>::AppendString(
     const SrcChar* chars, size_t length,
     const DisallowGarbageCollection& no_gc) {
-  constexpr int kUseSimdLengthThreshold = 32;
-  if (length >= kUseSimdLengthThreshold) {
-    return AppendStringSIMD(chars, length, no_gc);
+  // AppendStringSIMD builds a hw::FixedTag<SrcChar, 16>, i.e. it requires a
+  // target that can provide a 16-lane byte vector. Highway falls back to
+  // HWY_SCALAR (HWY_LANES(T) == 1) whenever neither a native SIMD target nor
+  // EMU128 is available, which is the case for riscv64 without the V extension
+  // when built with GCC: HWY_RVV is excluded and HWY_BROKEN_EMU128 is set for
+  // GCC < 16, leaving HWY_SCALAR as the static target. Instantiating the SIMD
+  // path there fails to compile:
+  //
+  //   shared-inl.h:369:27: error: static assertion failed: Too many lanes
+  //     note: the comparison reduces to '(16 <= 1)'
+  //   shared-inl.h:234:24: error: static assertion failed: Out of range
+  //     note: the comparison reduces to '(16 <= 8)'
+  //
+  // Only instantiate it when the static target can satisfy it. AppendStringSWAR
+  // below is a complete fallback and already handles arbitrary lengths, so this
+  // costs nothing but throughput on such targets. On every target that does
+  // provide 16-byte vectors the generated code is unchanged.
+  if constexpr (HWY_LANES(SrcChar) >= 16) {
+    constexpr int kUseSimdLengthThreshold = 32;
+    if (length >= kUseSimdLengthThreshold) {
+      return AppendStringSIMD(chars, length, no_gc);
+    }
   }
   return AppendStringSWAR(chars, length, 0, 0, no_gc);
 }
